Falsifies `system_tests::user::tests::a_name_resolves_through_the_stack_and_a_real_one_when_the_host_answers`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: `Query::accept` takes every class-IN A record in the answer, not only those owned by
the end of the canonical name chain from the name asked. That is cache poisoning in one line: a reply about
one name plants an address the server gave for another.

Expected to fail: the gating assertion, with client code `0xe14f` (case 4, `poisoned.nife.test`,
a wrong verdict). Measured 2026-10-04 (UTC) on aarch64: red with exactly that code.

